      "problem": "$\\int (2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int (-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
